<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kondh</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Khonds, Kandha, Kondh people</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kondh are an Adivasi people of the hills and forests of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, speaking the Dravidian languages Kui and Kuvi. They are the largest tribal community in Odisha. In the 1830s and 1840s British officials campaigned to end their meriah <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/human-sacrifice">human sacrifices</a>, and their lands lay in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> such as Kalahandi, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patna">Patna</a> and Baudh.</p></div>
